Yeah, I know, it's a valk, I'm not bragging about ascending her.

That over with, this is the luckiest game I've had in my life. I got
Excalibur early on, and hit two bones piles soon after, both of which
had magic markers and a good assortment of scrolls, and even a cloak
of MR. Killed a unicorn quickly, found two pairs of cursed gloves in
the piles and kept them for a while. I got Mjollnir and some holy
water after converting the Minetown altar by polymorphing the priest
into a Green-elf. Guess what kind of gloves those were? Gauntlets of
power. I quickly advanced my hammer skill to expert as well, and
destroyed everything for the next few levels with both of them.

A ways down, I polypiled some of my spare unihorns and got another
magic marker (unfortunately, I later wasted a scroll of charging,
having forgotten that I had polypiled it and that polypiled markers
can't be recharged). I found a magic lamp in a general store, and soon
after a large jewellers. Once I got a blessed ?oID on them, I
discovered that every good ring was in the shop except free action
(which I convieniently found on the next level). I had already reached
level 14 by the time I hit the quest portal, and had 3 wands of
polymorph and a ring of polymorph control, so I polymorphed myself
into a vampire lord and did the quest easily. Having found a cursed
scroll of genocide, I reverse genocided silver dragons and made myself
some SDSM for the one remaining important item I was missing.

I reached Medusa soon after, found the titan peaceful, and levitated
across the water to Medusa. She death-dropped (you guessed it!) a wand
of wishing, which I found out rather to my surprise when I engrave-
tested it. I dug down through the next couple of maze levels and
reached the castle, where I found out somewhat to my annoyance that I
didn't have an instrument. However, I had poly control, so I
polyselfed into a xorn, grabbed the second /oWishing, looked through
the stores, polymorphed again into a master mind flayer, and cleared
out the throne room. I wrote loads of scrolls, then levelported up to
sokoban, reverse genocided leprechauns for teleportitis, did some
nurse dancing, and wished for a blessed figurine of an archon. It took
me three tries to get a tame one, but I had spare wishes (if I hadn't,
having one wouldn't have even crossed my mind, as a valk).

I found Fort Ludios (my last three games didn't have it, so it was
nice for a change), leveled up my archon to level 28, killed
everything, and hauled the gold down to the Valley for 6 points of
protection, then mapped Gehennom quickly. The ascension run was
straightforward; I polymorphed into a master mind flayer for most of
it just for fun. Should I add that the mysterious force only brought
me down 5 levels total despite being lawful?

Now why can't I have had such a lucky game with a harder role than
valk?

